❌ The X account @indiantiwari01 is circulating fake claims stating that on the night of September 20, 2026, eight Indian Army personnel were killed in clashes and that the Army was firing directly, further worsening the situation and increasing tensions in the region.

✅ FACT: The claims that 8 Indian Army personnel were killed in clashes and that the Indian Army was directly firing are totally false.

✅ The video in the fake post is actually related to eruption of protests after security forces detained seven people suspected of links to an armed militant group in Kangpokpi. Protesters blocked NH-2, burnt tyres and clashed with security forces. The detained villagers were later released and situation came under control. 

